  "description": "Financial primitives for .NET. Provides Money (runtime-tagged primary monetary type), Money<TCurrency> (opt-in type-parameter currency safety with implicit conversion to and explicit conversion from the runtime form), MoneyBag (mixed-currency portfolios), CurrencyInfo and CurrencyCode (canonical metadata and a source-generated ISO 4217 enum covering every shipped code, active and historic), CurrencyRegistry (runtime lookup), and a foreign-exchange provider stack with both runtime ExchangeRate and typed ExchangeRate<TBase, TQuote>. Ships the active ISO 4217 currencies (fund and special-purpose codes excluded) plus 29 historic ones, cash rounding (CHF/AUD/CAD/NZD/SEK/NOK), and an exact-arithmetic escape hatch through Fraction<BigInteger> from Bodu.Numerics.",
